<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alhama de Granada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alhama de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> is a town in the province of Granada, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, known since Roman and Moorish times for its hot springs. A Nasrid stronghold guarding the road to Granada, it was taken by a Castilian surprise attack in February 1482, in reply to the Nasrid seizure of Zahara, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a> that ended with the fall of Granada in 1492.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhama-de-granada.jpg" alt="Alhama de Granada" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andaluc%C3%ADa_AlhamaDeGranada3_tango7174.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
